            "content": [
              {
                "type": "output_text",
                "text": "Here’s what’s **newest today (Monday, August 3, 2026)** around **Azure AI**—based on the most recent official Microsoft sources and major coverage.\n\n## 1) The best “today” source: Azure Updates (official)\nMicrosoft’s **Azure Updates** page is the canonical feed for same-day service announcements and rollouts across Azure (including Azure AI services / Azure AI Foundry / Azure OpenAI). If you want “today’s Azure AI news,” filtering here is usually the fastest way to see what actually shipped. ([azure.microsoft.com](https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/updates/))\n\n## 2) Most recent official Azure AI/Foundry announcements (late June–July 2026)\nOn the **Microsoft Azure Blog**, recent AI-related announcement headlines include:\n- **“GPT-5.6 now available in Microsoft Foundry”** (July 9, 2026). ([azure.microsoft.com](https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/blog/))  \n- **“Claude in Microsoft Foundry is now generally available”** (June 29, 2026). ([azure.microsoft.com](https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/blog/))  \n\nThese are among the latest “big platform” posts in the Azure blog feed, and they’re directly relevant to Azure AI / Foundry users. ([azure.microsoft.com](https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/blog/))\n\n## 3) Latest “What’s new” for Azure OpenAI / Foundry Models (official docs)\nMicrosoft’s “What’s new” page for **Azure OpenAI in Microsoft Foundry Models (classic)** summarizes recent releases/notes, including updates around **realtime and audio models** (latest section shown is **May 2026**). ([learn.microsoft.com](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/foundry-classic/openai/whats-new))\n\n## 4) Broader Microsoft Cloud/Azure business news (context)\nIn broader reporting “today,” there are articles framing Azure/Microsoft’s AI momentum around earnings and cloud performance (useful context, but not always “Azure AI product” changes). ([crn.com](https://www.crn.com/news/cloud/2026/aws-vs-microsoft-vs-google-cloud-earnings-q2-2026-face-off))\n\n---\n\nIf you tell me which part of “Azure AI” you mean (Azure AI Foundry, Azure OpenAI, Azure AI Search, AI Services like Vision/Language, etc.), I can narrow this to **only items posted/updated on August 3, 2026** and summarize just those.",
